    "long": "Swabian Acquisition is a Boise, Idaho company formed to buy one established business in the Treasure Valley and own it for the long term. Jeff Richardson, the Owner, is looking for a business in Ada or Canyon County with at least $1 million in annual revenue, preferably a B2B or commercial services company that has operated five or more years. Swabian is not a fund, a broker, or a search vehicle. After a purchase, Swabian puts professional management in place and works with the seller on what happens to the company: who runs it, the timeline, staffing and key people, the company name, and the seller's own role after close."
